{
  "name": "slip-roll-slide",
  "description": "The three clip-level moves that do not change where a clip sits as a whole, driven through the real app with positional assertions. Each step names the clip by the span its own semantics label reports and then asserts the span after the move, and the slip step also asserts the source window, because a slip changes nothing else. This is the difference between proving the app accepted a command and proving it left the clips where the operation says it should.",
